## Setup and Execution

### 1. Prerequisites
- Python 3.9+ on Windows, macOS, or Linux[cite: 91].

### 2. Install Dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
*(Or directly: `pip install pygame numpy networkx`)*[cite: 91]

### 3. Run the Simulation
```bash
python main.py
```

## Controls
| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Arrow Keys** (`Up`, `Down`, `Left`, `Right`) | Drive the robot (`BLUE` circle) through the arena and build `TopologicalMemory` (`RED` place-cell nodes, `GRAY` edges)[cite: 91] |
| **`P`** | Run simultaneous `TopologicalMemory` and `GridAStar` path queries, print `[BENCHMARK]` metrics to the console, and draw the `GREEN` (topological) and `ORANGE` (Grid A\*) paths[cite: 91] |
| **`ESC` / Close Window** | Exit the simulation[cite: 91] |

## Default Parameters
| Parameter | Default Value | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `step_threshold` | `45.0` px | Minimum Euclidean distance before creating a new topological place-cell node[cite: 91] |
| `connect_radius` | `80.0` px | Maximum distance to add a line-of-sight loop-closure shortcut edge to an earlier node[cite: 91] |
| `cell_size` | `20` px | Grid cell width/height for the `30 x 40` (`1,200`-cell) `GridAStar` occupancy map[cite: 91] |
| `clearance` | `12` px | Obstacle inflation margin (matches `Robot.radius`)[cite: 91] |

## Benchmark Trade-Off Overview
- **`TopologicalMemory`:** Operates over a sparse graph (`O(V log V + E)` shortest-path lookup), typically yielding **lower search latency**, though path cost can be higher than a direct grid route when shortcuts or shorter node sequences are not yet present/selected[cite: 91].
- **`GridAStar`:** Searches a denser discretized grid (`O(N log N)` over `1,200` cells), typically yielding **shorter, more direct obstacle-avoiding routes** at higher compute and memory cost[cite: 91].
